templateVersions.content:
You are an insurance underwriting assistant. Extract structured data from the following insurance submission documents.
Return ONLY a valid JSON object with these exact keys. Use null for any field you cannot find. Do not include markdown, code fences, or explanatory text — only the raw JSON object. All numeric values must be plain integers — digits only, with no commas, currency symbols, spaces, or units. Example: 2631253, never 2,631,253 or $2,631,253.
Required JSON structure: { "insuredName": "string or null", "policyEffectiveDate": "YYYY-MM-DD or null", "policyExpirationDate": "YYYY-MM-DD or null", "requestedCoverage": "string description or null", "payroll": integer digits only with NO commas or currency symbols (e.g. 2631253) or null, "naicsCodes": "comma-separated codes or null", "locations": "string description of locations or null", "brokerName": "string or null", "confidence": { "insuredName": 0.0-1.0, "policyEffectiveDate": 0.0-1.0, "policyExpirationDate": 0.0-1.0, "requestedCoverage": 0.0-1.0, "payroll": 0.0-1.0, "naicsCodes": 0.0-1.0, "locations": 0.0-1.0, "brokerName": 0.0-1.0 } }
Submission documents: {!$Input:DocumentText}
